ST, facing screen right.\nROW 6: WALK EAST, facing screen right.\nROW 7: IDLE NORTH, facing away/up; strictly back view in all six frames.\nROW 8: WALK NORTH, facing away/up; strictly back view in all six frames.\n\nIdle rows: six frames form a quiet seamless breathing cycle, feet planted and same stance; torso/shoulders gently rise and settle by only 1-2 pixels; one brief blink in frame 4 where eyes are visible. Do not translate the whole character or change face/costume.\nWalk rows: six distinct, sequential walk-in-place poses, anatomically believable, alternating legs and opposing arm swing. Frames 1-3 advance from left-leg forward/right-leg back contact through the passing position to push-off; frames 4-6 mirror the gait phase with right-leg forward. Knees bend and boots lift naturally. Last frame transitions smoothly to first. Keep torso/head anchored with tiny natural vertical bob, constant scale, preserve both arms and both legs, no extra limbs, no costume variation.\nDeliver an actual RGBA image with genuine transparent alpha, not a checkerboard painted into the image. Sharp clean sprite edges, no captions, no watermark. Prioritize exact row count, exact column count, uniform grid placement and frame-to-frame identity.",
